        {
            "id": "https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/12791",
            "content_html": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">What is the new suggestion?</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Webcodecs introduce ImageDecoder and ImageDecoder come with ImageTrackList.<br>\nIt sounds like a nice feature but I can't figure out how to provide an image file containing multiple tracks...<br>\nI even never heard about tracks inside an image and google doesn't help me at all with that.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">ImageTrackList exists so I'm sure it's doable but how to package multiple tracks inside a single image file ?</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Why is it important or useful?</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think it would be a great way to organised assets compared to a spritesheet but I have no idea how to create the multi-tracks-image.  What tool am I suppose to use ?  What would be the format of the file ?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\"Does it address critical needs in the web industry?\"<br>\nProbably not but this feature existed in Adobe Flash (the ability to package multiple assets, easy to target, inside a single file) and I really miss it. The idea I could do it again soon with ImageDecoder &amp; ImageTrackList makes me very happy. Please show us a step by step example to create such images .</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN URL: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/</a><br>\nMDN URL: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/TextEncoder\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/TextEncoder</a></p>",
